{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Thus, etc.</b> The prophet returns to rebuke the wicked." "<b>The heavens are My throne.</b> We know that the glory of HaShem fills the heavens and the earth, and the meaning is that decrees come forth from the heavens upon the entire world, just as they go forth from before a king when he sits on his throne." "<b>The footstool of My feet.</b> For it is under My dominion and Mine; and since all is Mine — what house?" "<b>And what place.</b> Doubled in meaning."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:08.633948757Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}